# US Business Phone Number Collection Agent

## Goal and scope

Continuous background agent that collects publicly listed US business phone numbers.

- **Primary**: Official structured APIs (Yelp Fusion, Google Places, Foursquare Places, OpenStreetMap/Overpass).
- **Secondary**: Limited crawling of specifically authorized sites only (permission-gated fallback).
- **Output**: Growing, clean DB of unique US phones with provenance (source, business name, address, category, timestamps, validation).
- Stay within free/approved quotas and company permissions. Prefer APIs over scraping.

## Stack

Django (models, admin, tasks) + Celery (or Django-Q) + Redis + PostgreSQL.

## Architecture layers

1. **Source Registry** — catalogue of APIs + approved websites (credentials, quotas, params, priority, last run).
2. **Acquisition** — API clients first; optional polite crawler for approved sites only.
3. **Normalization & Validation** — E.164 US numbers; reject invalid; area-code → state when possible.
4. **Storage & Deduplication** — unique E.164 key; merge context on re-see; keep raw payload for audit.
5. **Enrichment** (optional) — free validation, line-type, geography, risk; rate-limited.
6. **Orchestration** — schedule jobs, quotas, health, internal admin/search.
7. **Audit & Compliance** — log every fetch; respect rate limits; record exact source.

## Source registry fields

Name, type (API|website), credentials (secure), free/approved quotas + reset times, allowed query params (cities, categories, radius, pagination), priority, last successful run, data-quality notes. Scheduler only runs active sources with remaining quota.

### Primary sources

| Source | Notes |
|--------|--------|
| Yelp Fusion / Places | High-quality structured records; limited free calls (often hundreds/day). Best quality start. |
| Google Places | Highest completeness; free caps per SKU; phone often higher-cost SKU. |
| Foursquare Places | Phones often Pro tier; free often hundreds/month. |
| OSM / Overpass | Fully free, no key; incomplete phone coverage; highest free volume. |
| Authorized websites | Explicit permission only; low-priority fallback. |

## Acquisition flow

1. **Job trigger** — daily/hourly/on-demand; pick next eligible source (priority, quota, last-run).
2. **Query construction** — city/bbox + category; optional radius/text; pagination (offset/limit/next-page token). Overpass: area + tags (`phone`, `contact:phone`, amenity/shop).
3. **Fetch** — authenticated/public requests; JSON/XML; obey rate-limit headers; log failures; resume from page token.
4. **Extract** — phone(s), name, address/city/state/postal, category, source ID/URL, extras (hours, website, rating). Pass candidates with full context downstream.
5. **Website fallback** (if authorized) — approved sections only; polite delays; headless only if needed; extract phones + surrounding text into same candidate shape.

## Normalization & validation

1. Strip decorative chars, extensions, noise.
2. Parse as US (+1).
3. Convert to E.164.
4. Reject bad length/area-code/validity.
5. Extract area code → state via public tables when possible.
6. Keep original raw text + source context.

Only clean valid US numbers proceed.

## Storage & deduplication

Store: E.164 (unique), national format, source + exact query/page, business context, first/last seen, validation/enrichment status, raw payload. On reappearance: update last-seen and append context — no duplicate rows.

## Enrichment (optional, rate-limited)

Offline formatting/line-type hints; free-tier validators (e.g. DialCode ~1k/month); public area-code geography. Write results back onto same records; never exhaust free quotas.

## Orchestration & monitoring

Rotate sources by remaining quota + priority; check quotas before run, update after response. Metrics: yield per source, success rate, quota burn, API/structure errors. Alerts: format change, quota nearly exhausted, sharp yield drop. Admin: enable/disable sources, harvest stats, search by area code/state/source/date, manual targeted runs. Full audit logs.

## Free limits strategy

OSM = bulk free volume. Yelp/Google/Foursquare used first for quality; back off when free calls low. Merge + dedupe across sources. Cache within each API’s allowed window. When commercial free capacity is exhausted, continue with OSM + authorized sites until reset.

## Daily / continuous cycle

Scheduler → eligible sources → structured queries → extract → E.164 validate → unique store + provenance → parallel enrichment → metrics/quotas → repeat.

## Operational safeguards

Strict quota/rate-limit obedience; full provenance; dedupe; instant pause per source; audit trail; APIs preferred over scraping.
